# {{app_title}}

A [Plotly Dash](https://dash.plotly.com) dashboard with a
[Dash Bootstrap Components](https://dash-bootstrap-components.opensource.faculty.ai)
sidebar layout, scaffolded with
[dash-init](https://github.com/budescode/dash-app) on {{create_date}}.

## Run it

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
```

Or with [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (reads `pyproject.toml`):

```bash
uv sync
uv run app.py
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:8050 in your browser.

## What's inside

- **Responsive 12-column grid**: sidebar (`md=3`) + content (`md=9`), stacks on mobile
- **KPI cards** that update together with the chart from one callback
- **FLATLY theme + Bootstrap Icons** loaded via `external_stylesheets`,
  swap `dbc.themes.FLATLY` for any of the ~25 bundled themes

## Project layout

| Path               | Purpose                                     |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |
| `app.py`           | Layout (sidebar + cards + chart) + callback |
| `requirements.txt` | Python dependencies (pip)                   |
| `pyproject.toml`   | Same deps + metadata (uv, poetry)           |

## Deploy

**Plotly Cloud**, the official hosting, free tier available:

```bash
pip install "dash[cloud]"
plotly user login
plotly app publish
```

The first publish creates a `plotly-cloud.toml` here; commit it, so future
publishes update the same app. Re-publish anytime with `plotly app publish`.

**Any WSGI host**: `app.py` exposes `server = app.server`:

```bash
pip install gunicorn
gunicorn app:server
```
